--[[--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Lunchbox Toolkit — TalentValues
    Static data pack for the /lbs talent valuation layer. Loaded like the other
    data files (see LunchboxToolkit.toc); no frames, no client API, data only.

    PROVISIONAL — coefficients get tuned in Forever beta patches and are not
    always reflected in the in-game tooltip immediately. Revisit every number
    here against Forever blueposts / patch notes before release.
      * Shaman is the provisionally-working class (quality = "provisional").
      * Every other class is quality = "beta".
      * `quality` is metadata about how much to trust the derived `kind` /
        valuation, NOT about the raw tooltip text: `rt` (f + v) is always
        carried intact and is the source of truth for what the client shows.

    Delta source: foreverchanges.pro (per-class vs Classic), beta build
    1.60.1.70707. The Forever tree diverged heavily from Classic; talents whose
    `classic` flag is "new" are new in Forever, "moved" moved (old location in
    `cwas`), "changed" changed, "same" unchanged. Removed-from-Classic talents
    are NOT representable here (they are absent from the Forever tree).

    `kind` is a first-pass keyword classification of `rt.f` (falling back to the
    Classic text or the name for single-rank abilities with no rank tooltip).
    It is a small taxonomy, not a full EP model; a talent with several effects
    takes the first matching keyword. See TalentValues.kinds for the fixed set.

    `mentions` is the array of ability names a talent's effect is scoped to
    (lifted from TalentsForeverBook). A talent that affects everything carries
    no `mentions` field; an ability-scoped talent carries the specific names.

    Generated by tools/gen_talentvalues.lua from:
      * TalentsForeverBook 0.38.13 Data.lua (build 1.60.1.70425)
      * StatPriority 1.6.4 Data.lua (RatingPerPercent; its ForeverEP values
        are rebased to the canonical channels in this tool)
    Do not edit by hand: hand corrections live in TalentOverrides.lua, which
    loads after this file and patches it once.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------]]

